// gitdiff.nv — two blobs, compared, and how alike they are.
//
// Every body here is a `todo()`; the signatures are the design.
//
// THE DIFF IS diff-nv's, AND ONLY THE TOKENISATION AND THE SIMILARITY
// ARE HERE.  Tokenising two blobs and answering hunks is
// `diffscript.diff`; git's own diff is Myers with the same patience and
// histogram variants diff-nv already publishes, so a second
// implementation here would be a second thing to keep in step and a
// second set of hunks a renderer has to learn.  What git adds is
// deciding that a deleted path and an added path are one renamed file,
// and that is arithmetic over the scripts rather than a different
// algorithm.
//
// WHY THE BLOB SPLIT IS NOT `str.split`.  Git tokenises by line over
// BYTES, keeps the line terminator with the line, and treats a file
// with no trailing newline as a line of its own — so two blobs that
// differ only in the final newline differ in exactly one hunk, which is
// what `\ No newline at end of file` in a patch is reporting.  A
// tokeniser that split on `\n` and dropped the terminator makes that
// difference invisible and makes the patch it renders unappliable.
//
// NOTHING HERE PERFORMS ANYTHING.  Every row in this module is `[]`.

use diffscript

// The diff between two blobs, as diff-nv's script.
//
// Tokenised by line with git's own whitespace handling.  The hunks a
// caller renders are `diffscript.hunks`, so a tool that already renders
// a diff renders this one and nothing new is invented.
//
// ```novo
// use gitdiff
// use diffscript
//
// fn between(a: Bytes, b: Bytes) -> DiffScript
//     gitdiff.diff_blobs(a, b, diffscript.default_options())
//
// fn main() [io]
//     println("the change between two blobs")
// ```
pub fn diff_blobs(a: Bytes, b: Bytes, o: DiffOptions) -> DiffScript []
    todo("git-core-nv.gitdiff.diff_blobs")

// How alike two blobs are, as the percentage git computes.
//
// The number a rename carries and a similarity threshold compares
// against.  Published because rename detection is the part of a diff a
// person argues with — "that is not the same file" — and a tool that
// can show the percentage can be argued with productively.
//
// ```novo
// use gitdiff
//
// fn alike(a: Bytes, b: Bytes) -> Int
//     gitdiff.similarity(a, b)
//
// fn main() [io]
//     println("how alike two blobs are")
// ```
pub fn similarity(a: Bytes, b: Bytes) -> Int []
    todo("git-core-nv.gitdiff.similarity")

// Split two blobs into the lines git diffs them by, interned against
// each other.
//
// BOTH SIDES IN ONE CALL, because diff-nv's token ids only mean "the
// same token" when the two sides were interned into one table — two
// `DiffTokens` produced separately have unrelated ids and must not be
// diffed.  A single-blob tokeniser would publish exactly the value a
// caller is forbidden to use.
//
// The terminator stays with its line and a file with no final newline
// ends in a line of its own, which is what makes the missing newline a
// difference a patch can carry.  Published separately from `diff_blobs`
// so a caller that wants git's tokenisation under diff-nv's other entry
// points — the three-way merge, a patch applier — can have it.
//
// ```novo
// use gitdiff
//
// fn lines(a: Bytes, b: Bytes) -> DiffInput
//     gitdiff.tokenise_blobs(a, b)
//
// fn main() [io]
//     println("two blobs, as the lines git compares")
// ```
pub fn tokenise_blobs(a: Bytes, b: Bytes) -> DiffInput []
    todo("git-core-nv.gitdiff.tokenise_blobs")

// Would git treat this blob as binary?
//
// A NUL byte in the first 8000 is git's whole test, and it is the one
// that decides whether a diff is hunks or the line "Binary files
// differ".  Published because a tool that ran a line diff over a PNG
// produces megabytes of unreadable output, and because the threshold is
// a constant a reader should be able to see rather than guess.
//
// ```novo
// use gitdiff
//
// fn opaque(b: Bytes) -> Bool
//     gitdiff.is_binary(b)
//
// fn main() [io]
//     println("whether git would call a blob binary")
// ```
pub fn is_binary(b: Bytes) -> Bool []
    todo("git-core-nv.gitdiff.is_binary")
